## HARD RULES — NEVER VIOLATE THESE

1. NEVER rename tables, models, enums, modules, roles, or permission keys defined in the spec
2. NEVER put business logic in controllers — services only
3. NEVER put database calls in controllers — repositories only
4. NEVER bypass the service layer from controllers
5. NEVER place business logic in repositories — only query composition
6. NEVER weaken RBAC or remove permission checks
7. NEVER remove chat durability, notification durability, moderation, geolocation, or analytics
8. NEVER add payout or wallet settlement — out of scope for v1
9. NEVER invent new endpoints outside the 195-endpoint catalog without being asked
10. NEVER use HS256 for JWT — always RS256
11. NEVER store raw refresh tokens — always SHA-256 hash
12. NEVER auto-suspend users based on fraud score alone — human review required
13. NEVER write inline styles in frontend — Tailwind classes only
14. NEVER use StyleSheet.create in React Native — NativeWind className only

---

## MANDATORY ARCHITECTURE PATTERN

Every backend module MUST follow this exact pattern:

```
HTTP Request
    ↓
Controller (parse, validate with Zod, call service, return envelope)
    ↓
Validator (Zod schema — already defined in doc/zod-schemas.ts)
    ↓
Service (business logic, state machine guards, transaction boundaries)
    ↓
Repository / Prisma (query composition, pagination, typed results)
    ↓
EventBus.emit() (after successful write — BullMQ job enqueue)
```

---

## STANDARD RESPONSE ENVELOPES

```typescript
// ALL endpoints use these — no exceptions
Success:    { success: true,  data: {},         meta: { requestId, timestamp } }
Error:      { success: false, error: { code, message, details? }, meta: { requestId, timestamp } }
Paginated:  { success: true,  data: [],         pagination: { page, limit, total, hasNext }, meta: {} }
```

