## HOW TO USE CONTEXT FILES

When generating any backend module, ALWAYS start your prompt with:

```
@00_ARCHITECTURE.md @[relevant_module].md

Generate [module name] following the architecture rules above.
```

When generating any admin page, ALWAYS start with:

```
@admin_module_context_v2.md

Generate admin page [number]: [name]
Layout: Pattern [N] from design system
Endpoint: [from the module context]
Permission: [from the module context]
```

When generating any web page:

```
@VSP_Web_Frontend_Design_System.html (reference open in browser)

Generate web page [number]: [name]
Stack: Next.js 14, React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui
Font: Sora headings, DM Sans body
Brand: #0EA5E9 blue, #F97316 orange
Layout: Pattern [N] — [description]
Endpoint: [endpoint]
```

When generating any mobile screen:

```
@VSP_Mobile_Frontend_Design_System.html (reference open in browser)

Generate mobile screen [number]: [name]
Stack: React Native, Expo SDK 51, TypeScript, NativeWind
Font: Nunito headings, Inter body
Brand: #0EA5E9, Accent: #F97316
Navigator: [Tab/Stack] — [which navigator]
Endpoint: [endpoint]
```

