## TESTING STANDARDS

```typescript
// Every service method needs unit tests
// Use these fixture IDs — NEVER generate random UUIDs in tests

const IDs = {
  superAdmin:    'aaaaaaaa-0001-4000-a000-000000000001',
  admin:         'aaaaaaaa-0002-4000-a000-000000000002',
  moderator:     'aaaaaaaa-0003-4000-a000-000000000003',
  support:       'aaaaaaaa-0004-4000-a000-000000000004',
  customerAlice: 'aaaaaaaa-0005-4000-a000-000000000005',
  workerBob:     'aaaaaaaa-0006-4000-a000-000000000006',
  wpBob:         'bbbbbbbb-0001-4000-b000-000000000001',
  cityAccra:     'dddddddd-0001-4000-d000-000000000001',
  fixtureBooking:'ffffffff-0002-4000-f000-000000000002',
  fixtureReview: 'ffffffff-0003-4000-f000-000000000003',
}

// Key scenarios to always test per module:
// 1. Happy path — correct input → correct response
// 2. Permission denied — wrong role → 403 PERMISSION_DENIED
// 3. Not found — invalid ID → 404
// 4. State machine violation — wrong status → 422 REQUEST_INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION
// 5. Validation — missing required field → 422 VALIDATION_FAILED
// 6. Duplicate — idempotency key reuse → 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT (where applicable)
```

